## Theme Integration

### Theme Layouts
Page builder pages use theme layouts for consistent design.

**Layout Structure**:
```blade
<!-- resources/views/frontend/{theme}/layouts/page-builder.blade.php -->
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>{{ $page->title }}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="{{ $page->meta_description }}">
    <!-- Theme CSS -->
</head>
<body>
    @include('frontend.{theme}.partials.header')
    
    <main>
        {!! $pageContent !!}
    </main>
    
    @include('frontend.{theme}.partials.footer')
</body>
</html>
```

### Theme Switching
Pages can be assigned to specific themes:
- `default` - Default theme
- `blue` - Blue theme
- `light` - Light theme

When rendering, the appropriate theme layout is used.

## SEO Optimization

### Meta Tags
- Title tag (from `title` field)
- Meta description (from `meta_description` field)
- Meta keywords (from `meta_keywords` field)
- Open Graph tags (for social sharing)
- Twitter Card tags

### Sitemap Integration
Published pages automatically added to sitemap:
```xml
<url>
    <loc>https://example.com/{slug}</loc>
    <lastmod>{updated_at}</lastmod>
    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
    <priority>0.8</priority>
</url>
```

### URL Structure
- Clean URLs: `https://example.com/about` (not `/page/about`)
- Slug validation (lowercase, hyphens, no special chars)
- Automatic slug generation from page name

